# Favicon & brand identity assets

When the client logo or brand changes, **every** identity asset must be regenerated in the same task.
Never update one file and leave the others stale.

## Files to update — the complete checklist

| File | What it is | How to update |
|---|---|---|
| `public/favicon.svg` | Primary icon — used by all modern browsers | Edit SVG directly |
| `public/favicon.ico` | Fallback for legacy browsers | Regenerate via script (see below) |
| `public/apple-touch-icon.png` | iOS home-screen / Safari pinned tab — 180 × 180 | Regenerate via script |
| `src/assets/images/og-image.jpg` | Open Graph / Twitter card — 1200 × 630 | Regenerate via script |
| `src/config.yaml` → `metadata.openGraph.images[0].url` | Points to the OG image | Update path if filename changes |
| `src/config.yaml` → `metadata.title.default` / `template` | Site name in `<title>` tags | Update to match client |
| `src/components/Favicons.astro` → `mask-icon color` | Safari pinned-tab tint | Set to brand accent (`brand.colors.accent`) |

## Source of truth for the icon shape

The SVG source is **always based on the site logo** at `src/assets/images/logo.svg`.
Strip any `mix-blend-mode` / opacity effects — the icon must read on a solid background.

The `favicon.svg` structure:

```xml
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="-3 -3 49 37" width="32" height="32">
  <!-- dark brand background -->
  <rect x="-3" y="-3" width="49" height="37" rx="6" fill="[brand.colors.sectionDark]"/>
  <!-- logo paths in white — copied from logo.svg, mix-blend-mode removed -->
  <path d="…" fill="white"/>
</svg>
```

## Regeneration script

Run this **once** after changing the SVG. It uses `sharp` (already a project dependency).

```js
// scripts/gen-icons.mjs
import sharp from 'sharp';
import { readFileSync } from 'fs';

const BRAND_DARK = '#1B2A32';  // brand.colors.sectionDark

// Simple monogram SVG as fallback if the logo SVG has complex paths
// that librsvg can't parse (it rejects certain control characters).
const monogramSvg = (size, rx) => Buffer.from(
  `<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="${size}" height="${size}">` +
  `<rect width="${size}" height="${size}" rx="${rx}" fill="${BRAND_DARK}"/>` +
  `<text x="${size * 0.5}" y="${size * 0.72}" text-anchor="middle" ` +
  `font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="${Math.round(size * 0.49)}" fill="white">RA</text>` +
  `</svg>`
);

const ogSvg = Buffer.from(`<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1200" height="630">
  <rect width="1200" height="630" fill="${BRAND_DARK}"/>
  <rect x="70" y="60" width="200" height="260" rx="20" fill="#2C4A5B"/>
  <text x="170" y="228" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="130" fill="white">RA</text>
  <rect x="308" y="90" width="3" height="200" fill="#567F9B" opacity="0.5"/>
  <text x="340" y="160" font-family="Georgia,serif" font-size="72" fill="white">Rebellious Aging</text>
  <text x="342" y="220" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="28" fill="#7BA3BD">The science of living long — on your own terms.</text>
  <rect x="0" y="610" width="1200" height="4" fill="#567F9B" opacity="0.35"/>
</svg>`);

await Promise.all([
  sharp(monogramSvg(180, 36)).png().toFile('public/apple-touch-icon.png'),
  sharp(monogramSvg(32,  6 )).png().toFile('public/favicon.ico'),
  sharp(ogSvg).resize(1200, 630).jpeg({ quality: 92 }).toFile('src/assets/images/og-image.jpg'),
]);
console.log('✓ apple-touch-icon.png  ✓ favicon.ico  ✓ og-image.jpg');
```

Run it with:
```bash
node --env-file=.env scripts/gen-icons.mjs
```

## Config.yaml — always keep in sync

```yaml
metadata:
  title:
    default: Rebellious Aging          # ← client name
    template: '%s — Rebellious Aging'  # ← client name
  description: '…'                     # ← from Figma / SEO brief
  openGraph:
    site_name: Rebellious Aging        # ← client name
    images:
      - url: '~/assets/images/og-image.jpg'
        width: 1200
        height: 630
```

## Favicons.astro — mask-icon tint

```astro
<link rel="mask-icon" href="/favicon.svg" color="[brand.colors.accent]" />
```
Always use the brand accent colour (`brand.colors.accent` from `src/brand.ts`), not a hardcoded hex.

## Do not

- Update only `favicon.svg` and leave `.ico` / `apple-touch-icon.png` stale
- Reference `logo.webp` (old R&C Roofing asset — deleted) anywhere in `config.yaml` or meta tags
- Hardcode `#EDD974` or any non-brand colour in `mask-icon`
- Use the Figma MCP localhost image server URLs in any production asset
- Commit a 1024 × 124 logo as the OG image — OG cards must be 1200 × 630
